wildos-remote (0.1.6) trixie; urgency=medium

  * All my monitors lays the remote desktop out with each screen beside
    the same neighbour as here, in its own pixels. Screens with different
    scales were placed by multiplying their position by their own scale,
    which put them on top of each other, and each screen's window showed
    the wrong part of the desktop when the primary was not top left.
  * Built with the engine's monitor layout code from wildos-rdp 0.1.14.
  * All my monitors fills every screen: each monitor's window goes full
    screen on its own screen, at that screen's size. They all opened on the
    first screen, sized for every screen together, with their part of the
    desktop shrunk inside.

